f:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-navy-900 text-white py-16 md:py-20","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"font-display text-5xl md:text-7xl mb-6 tracking-wide","children":"OIL & GAS"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed","children":"Upstream exploration through downstream distribution and regulatory reporting"}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"py-20 bg-white","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[70ch]","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl text-navy-900 mb-6","children":"WHAT IT FEELS LIKE"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-gold-600 h-1 w-24 mb-8"}],[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6","children":"The price is set by the market. The geology is set by nature. The only thing the operation controls is how efficiently it converts reservoir energy into revenue. And that efficiency is determined by processes that most operators manage by exception rather than by design."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6","children":"Production operations run on well-level economics that change daily. Artificial lift optimization is reactive — wells decline and the response triggers when production drops below a threshold that was set when the well was new. Workover decisions are based on estimates and experience rather than integrated data. Lease operating expenses creep up because nobody owns the process of driving them down."}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6","children":"Midstream operations move product from wellhead to market through a network of gathering systems, processing plants, and pipelines. Scheduling, measurement, and allocation are technically sophisticated but operationally fragmented. Measurement discrepancies between custody transfer points create balancing issues that are \"normal\" — until audit reveals they’re not."}],["$","p","3",{"className":"text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6","children":"The operation produces and delivers hydrocarbons. But the spread between revenue and lifting cost — the only number that actually matters — is wider than it needs to be, and the processes that determine it are running on institutional knowledge rather than operational discipline."}]]]}]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"py-20 bg-gray-50","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl text-navy-900 mb-6","children":["PROCESSES: ","OIL & GAS"," OPERATIONS"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-gold-600 h-1 w-24 mb-12"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 p-8 hover:border-gold-600 transition-colors","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl text-navy-900 font-bold mb-3","children":"Well Planning & Permitting"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Designing well programs and securing regulatory approvals for drilling and completion activities. The process where engineering design meets regulatory reality."}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 p-8 hover:border-gold-600 transition-colors","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl text-navy-900 font-bold mb-3","children":"Drilling & Completion Operations"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Executing well construction from spud to first production. The process where daily costs are measured in tens of thousands and where operational efficiency is the primary controllable variable."}]]}],"$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23"]}]]}]}],"$L24","$L25","$L26"]}]
